## STANDING LINES THAT APPLY (copied from /Volumes/DevMASTER/WEDNESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/STANDING_LINES.md and the R 64th brief; read the file's sections of the same names)
- **READY FOR QA / READY TO MERGE are ARTEFACTS:** a PR number, its head SHA read from origin in the same action, the ticket comment naming the PR, the Test Evidence block you RAN, and what was NOT done. A sentence naming a SHA and no PR number is not ready.
- **INSTRUMENTS:** redirect to a file and read it (`cmd > out 2>&1; rc=$?` then read `$rc` on its own line); never `| tail`/`| head` on the stream you diagnose from; macOS has NO `timeout`; zsh has no PIPESTATUS (`$pipestatus[1]`); never `echo =====` (zsh expands `=word`; use `echo ----`); a `pgrep -f` matches your own command line, so exclude your pid; a count through `| head` is a truncated count.
- **A VERDICT LINE IS A CLAIM ABOUT WHAT RAN:** print ratios, never "all"; a skipped leg is not a pass; the hook's `PREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE` goes in verbatim.
- **What did my branch change is a THREE-DOT question** (`git diff X...HEAD`, `merge-base`), never `X..HEAD` on a branch you may be behind.
- **A TAMPER'S RESTORE NEEDS A UNIQUE ANCHOR:** `grep -c` the anchor = 1 before; after, count 1 again plus the whole-file sha256 equal to the pre-tamper hash. A mutant must PARSE before it runs, and a mutant copy under `src/__tests__` is type-checked by the ratchet: keep copies outside it. (Your red-first for A and B is by APPLYING the test without the product hunk, so there is no tamper; if you add one, it follows this line.)
- **PUSH-WINDOW LOCK + queue (Secuura/Blockchain on one laptop):** join the queue once per push (`T=$(PUSH_QUEUE_PID=<your waiter pid> bash /Volumes/DevMASTER/WEDNESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/push_queue.sh join "Seat R 65th")`; poll `push_queue.sh turn "$T"`; THEN `mkdir <Project>/worktrees/.push-lock` + a holder line; hold only on YOUR OWN successful `mkdir` (a flag set inside the loop on the mkdir that succeeded, never re-derived from the directory existing); with it held `pgrep -fl '^/bin/sh [.]githooks/pre-push origin git@github[.]com:'` must print nothing and load1 < 16; release only after the push rc and an `ls-remote` are in hand; `push_queue.sh leave "$T"`). Glob every `.push-lock-*` in `worktrees/` before any WAIT; an unknown one is a STOP naming it. Quarantine predecessor runtime artefacts after a port (`*-push.{start,end,rc}`, `.my-last-release`). Before each push re-read the open-PR file lists with a PLANTED CONTROL (a file list that DOES contain a path the matcher must flag; a zero without a firing control means nothing). If an open PR touches `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/Dockerfile`, anchoring `src/index.ts` lines :975-990, or `Blockchain/Dev/DEVELOPMENT.md`, STOP and mail.
- **STOP ONLY PROCESSES YOU STARTED, BY THE PID YOU RECORDED** (Wednesday 2026-10-28, ledger gate-pkill row): never `pkill`/`killall`/`kill $(pgrep ...)` by name; several seats run the same tools under the same names on one laptop. Arm every watcher as a TRACKED background task with the MAXIMUM background timeout (7200000 ms), note its re-arm deadline, claim a watcher RUNNING only on a `ps` reading taken in the same action; never a shell `&` in a foreground call; no foreground `sleep` polls.
- **A WORKTREE PATH IS ABSOLUTE AND NEVER UNDER THE CLONE.** A hung git on a stale `index.lock`: never remove a lock whose writer may be alive.
- **Fresh worktree: install and build `packages/shared` BEFORE the first push** (`npm ci --ignore-scripts` builds nothing; assert `dist/index.js`); a skip count above the box baseline (1: ks949) is a symptom.
- **Secuura test changes ship with the two Projects Documents html docs in the same commit** (skill section 4); seats appending concurrently merge develop in before each push and keep both sides' entries.
- **Client-facing communication is TICKET COMMENTS only.** Nothing to Peter or Stuart beyond a ticket comment. Signature classes (production, money, external communication, irreversible) pause for Kam.
- **Never delete** (quarantine into a dated folder and record the move); no `--no-verify`, no force push, no `--admin`; never `cd` (every path absolute); a gate that stops you is a question to answer, not a wall to route around.
- **Mail:** send from secuura-blockchain@ to `wednesday-agent@agentmail.to` ONLY, subject prefix `[Secuura/Blockchain-R -> Wednesday]`, body line 1 exactly `Seat R 65th`, no routing tokens (stop/hold/checkpoint) in a subject or mid-subject, no secrets; re-key `send_r64.py` to `_r65` (selftest) and read each sent mail back by id. Cadence: plan-confirmation (include the launcher preflight warnings VERBATIM, from `/Volumes/DevMASTER/!CODING/Secuura/Blockchain/4_Credentials/.launch_preflight_last.txt`, quoted with its launch stamp), READY FOR GATE per PR (A, then B), the C decision, and the wrap. Mid-session questions use `QUESTION: <topic>` with a mirrored-topic `ANSWER`; approval-class items always pause for Kam.
